WEBVTT

1
00:00:30.166 --> 00:00:33.958
<b>Now here, in the following verses,</b>

2
00:00:33.958 --> 00:00:35.916
<b>Lord Krishna explains</b>

3
00:00:35.916 --> 00:00:38.666
<b>that distancing oneself from action</b>

4
00:00:38.666 --> 00:00:42.583
<b>is not a suitable option for the soul,</b>

5
00:00:42.583 --> 00:00:47.166
<b>He states, by simply not performing actions.</b>

6
00:00:47.166 --> 00:00:49.833
<b>one cannot attain freedom </b>
<b>from the bonds of karma</b>

7
00:00:49.833 --> 00:00:56.500
<b>Nor can anyone achieve spiritual perfection </b>
<b>merely by renouncing everything.</b>

8
00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:00.291
<b>This emphasizes the importance of action.</b>

9
00:01:00.291 --> 00:01:03.291
<b>Let's understand this.</b>

10
00:01:07.958 --> 00:01:09.333
<b>In this verse,</b>

11
00:01:09.333 --> 00:01:11.708
<b>Krishna explains to Arjuna</b>

12
00:01:11.708 --> 00:01:14.458
<b>that a person whose mind is impure</b>

13
00:01:14.458 --> 00:01:19.041
<b>will be unable to attain the </b>
<b>supreme knowledge of the soul.</b>

14
00:01:19.041 --> 00:01:23.333
<b>If one thinks that merely not doing anything</b>

15
00:01:23.333 --> 00:01:27.083
<b>will free them from the </b>
<b>consequences of karmic bonds,</b>

16
00:01:27.083 --> 00:01:29.000
<b>it is a mistake.</b>

17
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.458
<b>Not performing any action</b>

18
00:01:31.458 --> 00:01:34.583
<b>is akin to running away</b>
<b>from one's responsibilities,</b>

19
00:01:34.583 --> 00:01:35.291
<b>and</b>

20
00:01:35.291 --> 00:01:38.166
<b>if you flee from your duties,</b>

21
00:01:38.166 --> 00:01:41.833
<b>you become a participant in wrongdoing.</b>

22
00:01:41.833 --> 00:01:43.625
<b>Lets understand it, this way.</b>

23
00:01:43.625 --> 00:01:50.875
<b>if a doctor flatly refuses to treat a </b>
<b>patient even in a serious condition,</b>

24
00:01:50.875 --> 00:01:54.416
<b>would they not be engaging in a bad deed?</b>

25
00:01:54.416 --> 00:01:55.791
<b>Imagine</b>

26
00:01:55.791 --> 00:02:00.750
<b>if the patient's health deteriorated or </b>
<b>something untoward happened.</b>

27
00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:05.958
<b>Could the doctor claim no involvement?</b>

28
00:02:05.958 --> 00:02:09.125
<b>He would certainly be </b>
<b>complicit in this poor outcome.</b>

29
00:02:09.125 --> 00:02:12.625
<b>It was his responsibility to treat the illness,</b>

30
00:02:12.625 --> 00:02:13.416
<b>but</b>

31
00:02:13.416 --> 00:02:16.166
<b>by denying his duty,</b>

32
00:02:16.166 --> 00:02:20.708
<b>he became a party to the wrongdoing.</b>

33
00:02:20.708 --> 00:02:22.916
<b>So, understand this clearly:</b>

34
00:02:22.916 --> 00:02:24.333
<b>not performing actions</b>

35
00:02:24.333 --> 00:02:27.000
<b>does not liberate one from karmic bonds.</b>

36
00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:29.666
<b>This applies to Arjuna as well.</b>

37
00:02:29.666 --> 00:02:34.375
<b>If, despite being a warrior, </b>
<b>he denies his duty to fight,</b>

38
00:02:34.375 --> 00:02:37.375
<b>he too will be a participant in wrongdoing.</b>

39
00:02:37.375 --> 00:02:40.791
<b>Because in such a case, he would </b>
<b>be neglecting his responsibility –</b>

40
00:02:40.791 --> 00:02:44.750
<b>not saving those he could have saved,</b>

41
00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:48.541
<b>not stopping the unrighteousness</b>
<b>he could have prevented.</b>

42
00:02:48.541 --> 00:02:50.416
<b>Isn't this a bad deed?</b>

43
00:02:50.416 --> 00:02:51.166
<b>Now,</b>

44
00:02:51.166 --> 00:02:54.666
<b>pay attention to the second part of the verse.</b>

45
00:02:54.666 --> 00:03:00.000
<b>Merely renouncing everything </b>
<b>does not lead to spiritual perfection.</b>

46
00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:01.666
<b>Arjuna had also said</b>

47
00:03:01.666 --> 00:03:06.583
<b>that he felt it would be better to </b>
<b>renounce everything and go to the forest,</b>

48
00:03:06.583 --> 00:03:12.250
<b>living the life of a renunciate, begging for alms.</b>

49
00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:13.166
<b>But</b>

50
00:03:13.166 --> 00:03:15.708
<b>is this his path to liberation?</b>

51
00:03:15.708 --> 00:03:16.750
<b>No,</b>

52
00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:18.250
<b>absolutely not.</b>

53
00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:20.208
<b>If the mind itself is impure,</b>

54
00:03:20.208 --> 00:03:23.625
<b>then renunciation and asceticism will </b>
<b>also fail in attaining liberation.</b>

55
00:03:23.625 --> 00:03:27.500
<b>Arjuna was not talking about going</b>
<b>to the forest with a peaceful mind;</b>

56
00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:34.916
<b>he was saying this out of fear of the death </b>
<b>of his relatives and the sin associated with it.</b>

57
00:03:34.916 --> 00:03:37.125
<b>So, if the mind is not at peace,</b>

58
00:03:37.125 --> 00:03:38.375
<b>not pure,</b>

59
00:03:38.375 --> 00:03:41.375
<b>what good will renunciation and asceticism do?</b>

60
00:03:41.375 --> 00:03:43.708
<b>Lets think of it this way,</b>

61
00:03:43.708 --> 00:03:50.958
<b>does a student become a complete doctor merely </b>
<b>by taking admission into a medical college?</b>

62
00:03:50.958 --> 00:03:52.125
<b>No, right?</b>

63
00:03:52.125 --> 00:03:57.500
<b>It requires hard work and years of practice.</b>

64
00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:00.250
<b>One has to face many difficulties.</b>

65
00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:05.583
<b>Only then will that person be </b>
<b>worthy of being called a skilled doctor.</b>

66
00:04:05.583 --> 00:04:06.625
<b>Similarly,</b>

67
00:04:06.625 --> 00:04:11.916
<b>merely entering into renunciation </b>
<b>and asceticism is not the path to liberation.</b>

68
00:04:11.916 --> 00:04:13.625
<b>Now the question arises:</b>

69
00:04:13.625 --> 00:04:16.666
<b>if giving up action is not the right path,</b>

70
00:04:16.666 --> 00:04:21.375
<b>and renunciation and asceticism </b>
<b>are also not the way to spiritual perfection,</b>

71
00:04:21.375 --> 00:04:24.625
<b>then what is the correct path?</b>

72
00:04:24.625 --> 00:04:29.708
<b>In both situations, it is clear that </b>
<b>one cannot escape from action.</b>

73
00:04:29.708 --> 00:04:34.250
<b>The complete path of </b>
<b>spirituality passes through action.</b>

74
00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:39.916
<b>And for this, purity of mind is also necessary.</b>

75
00:04:39.916 --> 00:04:47.333
<b>So, the best option is to follow the </b>
<b>path of action while purifying one's mind.</b>

76
00:04:47.333 --> 00:04:49.000
<b>And this can be achieved</b>

77
00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:51.291
<b>through the yoga of selfless action </b>
<b>(Nishkam Karma Yoga).</b>

78
00:04:51.291 --> 00:04:53.500
<b>Here, the duty will certainly be fulfilled,</b>

79
00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:55.166
<b>and at the same time,</b>

80
00:04:55.166 --> 00:04:59.458
<b>by renouncing attachment to the fruits of action, </b>
<b>the mind will also be purified.</b>

81
00:04:59.458 --> 00:05:02.791
<b>And as one progresses on </b>
<b>the path of Nishkam Karma Yoga,</b>

82
00:05:02.791 --> 00:05:04.625
<b>when the mind becomes pure,</b>

83
00:05:04.625 --> 00:05:10.750
<b>only then will the consideration of Gnana Yoga </b>
<b>or renunciation yield appropriate results.</b>

84
00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:15.625
<b>In the present situation, for Arjuna, </b>
<b>and for you as well, the essence is this:</b>

85
00:05:15.625 --> 00:05:18.208
<b>you must fulfill your responsibilities;</b>

86
00:05:18.208 --> 00:05:20.333
<b>you must perform actions.</b>

87
00:05:20.333 --> 00:05:21.125
<b>Yes,</b>

88
00:05:21.125 --> 00:05:23.958
<b>but action performed without desire for its fruits</b>

89
00:05:23.958 --> 00:05:28.250
<b>will certainly advance you </b>
<b>on the path of spirituality.</b>

90
00:05:28.250 --> 00:05:30.291
<b>Reflect upon this.</b>

91
00:05:34.708 --> 00:05:38.958
<b>Spirituality is a journey within the mind,</b>

92
00:05:38.958 --> 00:05:41.333
<b>not outside.</b>

93
00:05:41.333 --> 00:05:42.833
<b>But,</b>

94
00:05:42.833 --> 00:05:53.333
<b>often when practicing spirituality, people start </b>
<b>paying too much attention to external things.</b>

95
00:05:53.333 --> 00:05:55.916
<b>And they forget</b>

96
00:05:55.916 --> 00:06:03.291
<b>that merely changing external behaviors </b>
<b>and surroundings will not change the mind.</b>

97
00:06:03.291 --> 00:06:05.666
<b>For example,</b>

98
00:06:05.666 --> 00:06:09.500
<b>you must have seen people</b>

99
00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:12.208
<b>whose outward appearance,</b>

100
00:06:12.208 --> 00:06:15.583
<b>certain markings on the body,</b>

101
00:06:15.583 --> 00:06:17.625
<b>some rosaries, etc.,</b>

102
00:06:17.625 --> 00:06:23.666
<b>indicate that their inclination is spiritual.</b>

103
00:06:23.666 --> 00:06:25.291
<b>But</b>

104
00:06:25.291 --> 00:06:31.458
<b>sometimes there is a difference </b>
<b>between appearances and reality.</b>

105
00:06:31.458 --> 00:06:37.791
<b>Losing composure and expressing </b>
<b>anger at someone's small mistake,</b>

106
00:06:37.791 --> 00:06:44.541
<b>through spirituality, trying to </b>
<b>accumulate wealth and fame,</b>

107
00:06:44.541 --> 00:06:46.708
<b>and in many situations,</b>

108
00:06:46.708 --> 00:06:50.875
<b>secretly remaining engrossed in desires –</b>

109
00:06:50.875 --> 00:06:53.875
<b>if someone's mind is like this,</b>

110
00:06:53.875 --> 00:07:00.791
<b>then no special attire will make them spiritual.</b>

111
00:07:00.791 --> 00:07:02.083
<b>Whereas,</b>

112
00:07:02.083 --> 00:07:04.750
<b>The dilemma is that</b>

113
00:07:04.750 --> 00:07:13.416
<b>people often make the mistake of</b>
<b>considering external changes as spirituality.</b>

114
00:07:13.416 --> 00:07:16.125
<b>This doesn't mean</b>

115
00:07:16.125 --> 00:07:19.583
<b>that any particular attire is wrong.</b>

116
00:07:19.583 --> 00:07:23.000
<b>The point here is simply</b>

117
00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:27.083
<b>that mere external changes are not spirituality.</b>

118
00:07:27.083 --> 00:07:30.875
<b>The true meaning of real spirituality is</b>

119
00:07:30.875 --> 00:07:34.041
<b>purity of mind.</b>

120
00:07:34.041 --> 00:07:37.000
<b>And if the mind itself is not pure,</b>

121
00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:41.208
<b> then everything else is meaningless.</b>

122
00:07:41.208 --> 00:07:45.291
<b>As you embark on this spiritual journey,</b>

123
00:07:45.291 --> 00:07:47.125
<b>keep your focus</b>

124
00:07:47.125 --> 00:07:52.541
<b>on inner development and </b>
<b>purification of the mind.</b>

125
00:07:52.541 --> 00:07:58.208
<b>That is the true indicator of progress.</b>

126
00:08:02.666 --> 00:08:05.625
<b>There are all kinds of people in society.</b>

127
00:08:05.625 --> 00:08:06.791
<b>Those</b>

128
00:08:06.791 --> 00:08:15.916
<b>who understand well both, the truth </b>
<b>of spirituality and their social duties towards it.</b>

129
00:08:15.916 --> 00:08:16.625
<b>But</b>

130
00:08:16.625 --> 00:08:19.500
<b>there are also many people,</b>

131
00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:23.000
<b>many so-called gurus,</b>

132
00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:26.416
<b>who suggest inappropriate paths to people.</b>

133
00:08:26.416 --> 00:08:30.083
<b>Sometimes they even encourage others</b>

134
00:08:30.083 --> 00:08:36.583
<b>to give up their worldly </b>
<b>responsibilities prematurely.</b>

135
00:08:36.583 --> 00:08:38.416
<b>Inspired by this, </b>

136
00:08:38.416 --> 00:08:41.916
<b>some people either take sannyasa</b>

137
00:08:41.916 --> 00:08:48.666
<b>or start wearing the attire of ascetics.</b>

138
00:08:48.666 --> 00:08:51.166
<b>But</b>

139
00:08:51.166 --> 00:08:54.208
<b>if the mind remains impure,</b>

140
00:08:54.208 --> 00:09:02.083
<b>what difference will </b>
<b>sannyasa or such attire make?</b>

141
00:09:02.083 --> 00:09:04.583
<b>A person with a corrupt mind</b>

142
00:09:04.583 --> 00:09:11.541
<b>will inevitably engage in some unethical act.</b>

143
00:09:11.541 --> 00:09:14.541
<b>And it is because of such people</b>

144
00:09:14.541 --> 00:09:19.083
<b>that others lose faith in spirituality.</b>

145
00:09:19.083 --> 00:09:21.500
<b>The notion spreads</b>

146
00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:26.041
<b>that all this is a Pretense.</b>

147
00:09:26.041 --> 00:09:32.916
<b>What could be more detrimental </b>
<b>to spirituality than this?</b>

148
00:09:32.916 --> 00:09:39.166
<b>Spiritual knowledge is highly systematic</b>
<b>and methodical.</b>

149
00:09:39.166 --> 00:09:43.000
<b>By merely suggesting some superficial activities,</b>

150
00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:48.125
<b>You cannot awaken spirituality in someone.</b>

151
00:09:48.125 --> 00:09:51.208
<b>For a true spiritual experience,</b>

152
00:09:51.208 --> 00:09:56.125
<b>purity of mind is absolutely essential.</b>

153
00:09:56.125 --> 00:09:58.875
<b>And to attain this purity,</b>

154
00:09:58.875 --> 00:10:04.208
<b>one must pass through the process of action,</b>

155
00:10:04.208 --> 00:10:10.708
<b>performing selfless work without desire </b>
<b>for its fruits. Performing ‘Nishkam Karma’.</b>

156
00:10:10.708 --> 00:10:14.166
<b>The purification of gold extracted from a mine</b>

157
00:10:14.166 --> 00:10:19.500
<b>does not happen by just wiping or washing it.</b>

158
00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:23.666
<b>That gold has to burn in fire,</b>

159
00:10:23.666 --> 00:10:30.166
<b>only then will all its impurities</b>
<b>be reduced to ashes.</b>

160
00:10:30.166 --> 00:10:32.625
<b>Similarly,</b>

161
00:10:32.625 --> 00:10:40.791
<b>For purification, the mind may also </b>
<b>have to go through many difficult situations.</b>

162
00:10:40.791 --> 00:10:45.833
<b>Only then will its impurities be eliminated.</b>

163
00:10:45.833 --> 00:10:48.583
<b>The yoga of selfless action (Nishkam Karma Yog)</b>

164
00:10:48.583 --> 00:10:52.500
<b>is one path of this purification,</b>

165
00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:59.333
<b>and later on, the path of </b>
<b>Gnana Yoga may also open up.</b>

166
00:10:59.333 --> 00:11:02.916
<b>Which path is appropriate</b>

167
00:11:02.916 --> 00:11:07.291
<b>will depend on one's spiritual progress.</b>

168
00:11:11.708 --> 00:11:14.375
<b>In professional life often,</b>

169
00:11:14.375 --> 00:11:17.625
<b>such difficulties arise</b>

170
00:11:17.625 --> 00:11:22.500
<b>that one feels like escaping from them somehow.</b>

171
00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:29.500
<b>It seems that the only way to avoid </b>
<b>the pain is to run away from the situation.</b>

172
00:11:29.500 --> 00:11:31.000
<b>But</b>

173
00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:33.791
<b>the truth of life is</b>

174
00:11:33.791 --> 00:11:38.541
<b>that every situation has come with </b>
<b>the purpose of teaching you something,</b>

175
00:11:38.541 --> 00:11:42.833
<b>with the purpose of your progress, into your life.</b>

176
00:11:42.833 --> 00:11:46.625
<b>If you keep running away from situations like this,</b>

177
00:11:46.625 --> 00:11:49.750
<b>your growth will also stop.</b>

178
00:11:49.750 --> 00:11:51.375
<b>Therefore,</b>

179
00:11:51.375 --> 00:11:54.333
<b>do not run away from your problems;</b>

180
00:11:54.333 --> 00:11:55.416
<b>instead,</b>

181
00:11:55.416 --> 00:11:59.625
<b>learn to face them with full dedication.</b>

182
00:11:59.625 --> 00:12:02.375
<b>Ask yourself</b>

183
00:12:02.375 --> 00:12:06.125
<b>if fear is troubling you.</b>

184
00:12:06.125 --> 00:12:10.583
<b>Also, at the same time, </b>
<b>look into your past.</b>

185
00:12:10.583 --> 00:12:14.000
<b>You will find numerous examples</b>

186
00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:19.125
<b>where you were unnecessarily worried and afraid.</b>

187
00:12:19.125 --> 00:12:25.708
<b>Where you faced a difficulty </b>
<b>with courage and succeeded.</b>

188
00:12:25.708 --> 00:12:26.750
<b>Now,</b>

189
00:12:26.750 --> 00:12:31.500
<b>start working in the right direction </b>
<b>with self-confidence.</b>

190
00:12:31.500 --> 00:12:33.083
<b>Not the result,</b>

191
00:12:33.083 --> 00:12:34.250
<b>but</b>

192
00:12:34.250 --> 00:12:35.458
<b>action.</b>

193
00:12:35.458 --> 00:12:38.500
<b>Action is certainly in your control.</b>

194
00:12:38.500 --> 00:12:40.291
<b>Not the situation,</b>

195
00:12:40.291 --> 00:12:42.750
<b>but running away from it,</b>

196
00:12:42.750 --> 00:12:46.791
<b>or facing it and learning from it</b>

197
00:12:46.791 --> 00:12:49.833
<b>- this is in your control.</b>

198
00:12:49.833 --> 00:12:57.833
<b>You yourself know what is right between </b>
<b>these two options, don’t you?</b>

199
00:12:57.833 --> 00:12:59.708
<b>Reflect upon this.</b>

